 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“In Virginia prior to Bacon’s Rebellion we . . . have black planters and white planters, black indentured servants and slaves, we have white people who are indentured servants and living in un-freedom.</p>\n<p>In that kind of world, distinctions between black and white are of course made. But very few people talk about black people as being stupid or dull or ignorant or dirty or lazy. . . .</p>\n<p>When we move into the post-Bacon’s Rebellion world where slavery and the plantation economy are in place, where black people are arriving in large numbers from Africa, the view of black people changes very rapidly. It is not simply slavery that transforms notions of race. It is this plantation slavery, the advent of the plantation and disciplined, exploitative labor that begins to transform notions of race.</p>\n<p>And it is that which I am concerned with here. It’s not the origins of ideas of race but how race is continually transformed and giving different meanings in different circumstances.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Edited transcript, PBS Interview with Dr. Ira Berlin</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided</i>.</p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614781,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "According to the excerpt provided, which is most accurate description of colonial Virginia prior to Bacon’s Rebellion?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167098,
     "content_html": "Virginia in the 1600s had fewer racial stigmas than it did in the 1700s."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167097,
     "content_html": "Virginia was so heavily tied to the plantation system based on slave labor that no other form of labor existed in the colony."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167096,
     "content_html": "Africans were not permitted to enter the colony of Virginia."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167095,
     "content_html": "Virginia was a largely Catholic colony."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614782,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "According to the excerpt provided, what does Dr. Berlin believe the period after Bacon’s Rebellion brought about in Virginia?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167101,
     "content_html": "A diversified economy that saw industrialization begin to replace the slavery plantation system"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167100,
     "content_html": "A plantation system of agriculture that still largely relied on indentured servants as the prime labor force"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167099,
     "content_html": "A period of increased political rights and economic prosperity for blacks in the colony of Virginia"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167102,
     "content_html": "A colony dominated economically by a plantation system with a racially defined slave labor force"
    }
   ],
